# A genuinely missing /assets/* file must fail as a real 404, not fall through to
# the SPA rule below. Serving index.html (200, text/html) for a missing .svg/.png
# makes the browser render a broken image and hides the real "asset not deployed"
# problem (this is exactly what masked the taiga-ui icons being absent from a stale
# deploy). Real files are served before _redirects is consulted, so existing assets
# are unaffected — only truly-missing ones hit this.
/assets/*   /404.html     404

# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback: serve index.html for any client-side route so
# deep links (e.g. /live-training/admin, /{tenantId}/login) resolve instead of 404.
# Real files (JS, CSS, assets) are served directly; everything else falls through here.
/*          /index.html   200
